lgtm-autostart
==============

A local LGTM observability stack that starts automatically on macOS login.
Loki + Grafana + Tempo + OTel Collector, wired together with Docker Compose,
kicked off by a launchd agent so it's just there when you open your laptop.

Source: https://github.com/adarshba/lgtm-autostart


The problem
-----------

Every reboot meant manually starting the stack before any local telemetry
would be collected. Half the time the stack wasn't running and logs were
already lost. This repo fixes that.


Stack
-----

  OTel Collector   otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:0.99.0   port 4317, 4318
  Loki             grafana/loki:3.0.0                             port 3100
  Tempo            grafana/tempo:2.4.1                            port 3200
  Grafana          grafana/grafana:10.4.2                         port 3000

Grafana runs with anonymous admin — no login required.


Sending telemetry
-----------------

Point your OTel SDK at the collector:

  OTLP gRPC   localhost:4317
  OTLP HTTP   localhost:4318

Logs are routed to Loki. Traces are routed to Tempo.


macOS autostart
---------------

Copy the plist from example/ to your LaunchAgents folder:

  cp example/com.user.lgtm-autostart.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
  launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.user.lgtm-autostart.plist

Remove it:

  launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.user.lgtm-autostart.plist
  rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.user.lgtm-autostart.plist

Agent logs:

  /tmp/otel-stack.log
  /tmp/otel-stack.error.log


Manual start/stop
-----------------

  docker compose up -d
  docker compose down


File layout
-----------

  docker-compose.yml     service definitions
  loki.yml               Loki configuration
  otel-collector.yml     collector pipeline (OTLP → Loki + Tempo)
  tempo.yml              Tempo configuration
  example/
    com.user.lgtm-autostart.plist   launchd agent


Config changes
--------------

All config files are volume-mounted. Edit and restart:

  docker compose down && docker compose up -d


